Note (iv) - Papers which are to be preserved under the rules of this Chapter shall be repaired, where necessary, at the expenses of the Court; but documents which are filed by the parties in the High Court are filed in the Lower Court and transmitted to the High Court and which are ultimately returned to them after the disposal of the case in which they are filed shall be repaired, if and when necessary, at the expenses of the party filing such documents. An estimate of the cost of repairs shall be prepared and served on the advocate for the party and the amount due under the estimate shall be deposited with the accountant of the Court within seven days from the date of service. All cases of default as regards the deposit shall be reported to the Registrar. Rule 7 shall also apply mutatis mutandis, to the records of all Civil Revision cases and references. CRIMINAL RECORDS
